  "title": "Unified Title",
  "summary": "OpenSplatGraph provides a framework for structured scene graph generation from dense semantic maps, enabling open-vocabulary robot perception while maintaining geometric fidelity. ActiveLang enhances 3D mapping by incorporating semantic uncertainty and language adaptation, improving both scene understanding and human-robot interaction.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "OpenSplatGraph constructs persistent 3D scene graphs directly from an online Gaussian-based open-vocabulary semantic map.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "ActiveLang uses a dual-Gaussian representation to jointly reconstruct scene geometry, appearance, and open-vocabulary semantics with minimal memory overhead.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Experiments on Replica and ScanNet++ demonstrate significant improvements in 2D and 3D open-vocabulary segmentation.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
